<% content_for :title, "Aspect Ratio" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-violet-600 dark:text-violet-400">Components</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Aspect Ratio</h1>
  <p class="text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
    A box that holds its child at a fixed ratio. The child fills the box completely, whatever it is —
    an image, a video, or an embed.
  </p>
</div>

<%# Preview %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div id="aspect_ratio-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-neutral-900 flex flex-wrap items-start justify-center gap-6 p-8 mb-8">
  <% [
    [:square,   "Square · 1∶1"],
    [:video,    "Video · 16∶9"],
    [:portrait, "Portrait · 3∶4"],
    [:classic,  "Classic · 4∶3"],
  ].each do |ratio, label| %>
    <div class="w-40">
      <%= render Ui::AspectRatioComponent.new(ratio: ratio, class: "overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-border") do %>
        <div class="flex h-full w-full items-center justify-center bg-muted text-xs font-medium text-muted-foreground">
          <%= label %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# Usage %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#aspect_ratio-usage" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed"><code id="aspect_ratio-usage" class="text-neutral-200"><%= h(example_aspect_ratio_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<%# Options %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Options</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-neutral-50 dark:bg-neutral-900">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-neutral-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-neutral-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Type</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-neutral-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Default</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-neutral-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-neutral-100 dark:divide-neutral-800">
      <% [
        ["ratio", "Symbol", ":square", "One of :square, :video, :portrait, :classic."],
        ["class", "String", "nil",     "Merged over the ratio classes with tailwind_merge — pass an arbitrary aspect-[…] here for any ratio outside the fixed set."],
        ["…",     "Any",    "—",       "Every other keyword (id:, data:, aria:, …) is forwarded to the root element."],
      ].each do |name, type, default, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-neutral-50 dark:hover:bg-neutral-900/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-violet-600 dark:text-violet-400"><%= name %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-neutral-500"><%= type %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-neutral-400"><%= default %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# A ratio outside the fixed set %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">A ratio outside the fixed set</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-3">
  Tailwind only compiles a class it finds literally in the source, so <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">ratio:</code> only ever takes one of the four values above.
  Anything else — an ultrawide <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">21∶9</code>, say — comes from <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">class:</code> instead, which wins over the default:
</p>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed"><code class="text-neutral-200">&lt;%= render Ui::AspectRatioComponent.new(class: "aspect-[21/9]") do %&gt;…&lt;% end %&gt;</code></pre>
</div>

<%# Notes %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Notes</h2>
<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 list-disc list-inside">
  <li>The child is wrapped in an absolutely positioned, full-size inner box, so it fills the ratio whatever it is — no <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">h-full w-full</code> needed on an <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">&lt;img&gt;</code> or <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">&lt;iframe&gt;</code> you put inside it.</li>
  <li>A layout box only — nothing to announce. Give an <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">&lt;img&gt;</code> child its own <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">alt</code>.</li>
  <li>No Stimulus controller. Purely CSS, via the native <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">aspect-ratio</code> property.</li>
</ul>
